	(footprint "class_board:OLED-0.96in-4P-module-socket"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "8c611ab5-a0af-504a-8e87-e4de00717c1a")
		(at 151.05 74.92)
		(descr "0.96 in 128x64 I2C OLED module (4-pin GND VCC SCL SDA, 27 x 29 mm PCB (GM009605v4)) plugged into a vertical 1x4 2.54 mm female header 8.5 mm tall (XFCN PZ254-1-04-Z-8.5, LCSC C2894927); the module lies flat 11 mm above the board and is held by four M2 screws through its corner holes (2.4 mm holes at 24 x 26 mm, header body 1 mm below the top edge so the pin row is 2.27 mm below it and the top holes 0.77 mm above the pin row - the instructor's numbers, 2026-09-17, to be confirmed on the delivered modules; the housing front cover clamps the module anyway, Decision #61) into M2 stand-offs. Anchor = centre of the pad row (the socket, the part JLC places). Courtyard = socket + the four holes only: the module body hangs 11 mm above the board and may overhang other parts.")
		(tags "OLED SSD1306 0.96 module socket M2")
